{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310861,"nonce":"apO+KIAP01NrzC+r9+BS6PnpdPE=","title":".rzb bundle made a working self-contained production artifact (fix chain: finalize + --native-lib + tier-aware runner + cache-ignore). THE ...","message":"Prod runs as PACKAGED .rzb, not raw-haxe+cache (darmie). Made the .rzb path actually\nwork this session. Fix chain, all committed:\n\n- **7617e1ec** `fix(bundle)`: (a) preblade runs `finalize_mir_references()` before\n  snapshotting MIR (coherency pass AOT already runs; re-resolves cross-module CallDirect\n  by qualified name); (b) bundle the single MERGED module (`get_mir_modules().last()`) +\n  tree-shake + link stubs, mirroring run_file, NOT all un-merged modules; (c) new CLI\n  `--native-lib \u003cdylib\u003e` on `rayzor run` (run_file+run_bundle) loads raw kernel dylibs by\n  path = manifest `[build] native-libs` equivalent, so a .rzb runs with NO rayzor.toml;\n  (d) run_bundle runs `__vtable_init__`/`__init__` BEFORE `upgrade_to_llvm` (like run_file)\n  — `compile_all_with_llvm` only registers LLVM ptrs for functions already MATERIALIZED in\n  function_pointers, so without the inits the bundle was **0 LLVM / 100% Cranelift** in\n  --stats and decoded ~3x slow; after = 227 LLVM, parity.\n- **a0c527d1** `fix(bundle)`: `create_bundle` forces `enable_cache=false` — **THE root fix\n  for the 410017 SIGILL** (see below).\n- **0633174d** `bench(server)`: `BUNDLE=auto|\u003cpath\u003e` mode in bench_server.sh (socket server\n  in .rzb through the full stats pipeline; --native-lib + mirrored tier flags).\n\n`GGUFLoader.loadWithTokenizer -\u003e CallDirect fn 410017 \"not found in module\"` -\u003e LLVM upgrade\nfails -\u003e Cranelift trap-stub SIGILLs on first call (\"server did not reach listen\"). It is\n**DETERMINISTIC split by cache state**: cache-built server bundles **5/5 BAD**, `--no-cache`\n**15/15 clean**. Cached per-file MIR carries session-specific fn ids from the compile that\npopulated the cache; merged into the single bundle module a cross-module ref survives with a\nstale id that name-based finalize CANNOT remap. My earlier \"finalize fixed 410017, 14/14\"\nwas INCOMPLETE — llama-chat was built --no-cache so it never hit the cache path; the server's\n`BUNDLE=auto` (cached) crashed. NOT flag-triggered (same bundle works minimal AND full flags).\nFix = bundles never read/write the cache; compile fresh every time (cache still speeds `run`).\n\n`rayzor run app.rzb --native-lib libnue_plugins.dylib --preset application --release -- \u003cargs\u003e`\n- **--release REQUIRED**: bare `application` preset has enable_stack_traces=TRUE = ~19x\n  instrumentation (2.4 vs 45 tok/s). Manifest [tier] sets it false for free; standalone needs --release.\n- **--native-lib REQUIRED** if no rayzor.toml (supplies kernel symbols like\n  rayzor_kv_cache_q8_append). run_file resolves a manifest from the .rzb's dir/cwd if present.\n- Tier precedence (resolve_tier_config): manifest [tier] is base if present (preset IGNORED\n  unless --preset-override-toml); else CLI --preset. Then `--tier-thresholds` applied LAST =\n  OVERRIDES the base thresholds (preset does NOT override tier-thresholds — the reverse).\n  --preset defaults to \"application\" in clap even if omitted.\n\nready(launch-\u003elisten) bundle 4.2s vs source-from-compile 6.1s; cold_ttft 5.7s vs 7.7s; decode\n83 vs 79.5. Bundle skips the from-source front-end compile. That was the reason to bundle the server.\n\nSee [project-nuc-x86-target-thermal] (older BLOCKER note now resolved), [bugs-xmodule-resolution-disease-cluster].\n\n`.rzb` serializes `Vec\u003cIrModule\u003e`, so **any change to a MIR enum invalidates\nevery existing bundle**. Inserting `IrInstruction::VectorShuffle` ahead of the\n`Atomic*` variants shifted their postcard discriminants and every bundle built\nearlier failed with a bare `Serde Deserialization Error`.\n\nTwo things were wrong beyond the staleness itself:\n1. **The version guard was unreachable.** `magic`/`version` were checked AFTER\n   `postcard::from_bytes` had decoded the whole struct (payload included), so a\n   MIR change always failed in deserialization first. Now a `BundleHeader`\n   prefix is decoded and validated before the modules; a header-valid but\n   undecodable payload reports \"built by a different rayzor, rebuild it\".\n2. **`BUILD=1 ./run_bundle.sh` produced a BROKEN bundle.** It passed\n   `--no-cache` but never cleared `.rayzor` — and a stale `.blade` holds an\n   `IrModule` in the OLD layout that gets embedded into the new artifact.\n   `--no-cache` is not sufficient ([[feedback_blade_cache_clear_all_rayzor_dirs]]);\n   the script now clears every `.rayzor` first.\n\n**RULE: after ANY MIR/IR enum change, rebuild every `.rzb` and verify each one\nLOADS** — a clean build exit says nothing. The six: `nue/examples/llama-chat`,\n`nue/examples/llama-chat-server`, and `compiler/benchmarks/precompiled/{fibonacci,\nnbody,deltablue,mandelbrot}`. Rebuild: clear caches, then\n`rayzor bundle \u003csrc\u003e.hx -o \u003cname\u003e.rzb --no-cache`. Expected outputs:\nfib(40)=102334155, deltablue total=14065400, mandelbrot checksum=112798515.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_rzb_bundle_production_artifact` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}